                        


Item #:  SCP-5127

Object Class:  Safe

Special containment procedures: 

SCP-5127 is to be kept on a glass table inside a sealed 5x5 storage unit with no way of viewing it from outside due to its nature. There are to be no cameras inside and is only available for testing on D-Class Personnel unless approved otherwise by Class-B or higher individuals. Any tests conducted on this subject have to be backed up by a minimum of two Class-C or higher personnel who are not to be exposed to the effects of said object.

Exposure to SCP-5127 is to be minimized as much as possible, as short term negative effects are possible. After exposure, subjects are required to take a memory test.

It is to be watered 2 (two) times a day.

Description: 

SCP-5127 is a collection of multiple scorpion glass flowers (also known as “forget-me-not’s”) inside a tawny brown clay pot filled with sandy loam soil.

During visual exposure to SCP-5127, all brain cells in the exposed subject relating to memory will soften and loosen up in a way that will discard any memories that would have been created during visual exposure. This effect will continue around 5 (five) minutes after exposure, but will cease after. Should the subject still be in effect from SCP-5127 despite the passing of 10 (ten) minutes or longer, they are to be put into recovery and will no longer be eligible for testing, unless directed otherwise by the 05 council. Nausea during a state of recovery is common.

A subject visually exposed to SCP-5127 is to be temporarily referred to as “SCP-5127-1”, and so on, the number climbing as more people are exposed. Once a subject has fully recovered from SCP-5127 they will no longer be referred to as an SCP.

The origins of this SCP’s effects have not been found, the most popular hypothesis among our researchers is that SCP-5127 has a very specific microscopic pattern on it’s petals that toggles pressure points in the brain to result in such effect.

Due to its nature, tests are difficult to conduct on this subject as memory of the interactions with said object will be discarded. The current method consists of informing the Class-D to write down the newly acquired information while under the effect on a piece of standard paper. After the subject is no longer under the effect of SCP-5127, they are to review the document after being informed of what occurred to them, then if the document possesses no errors in the eyes of the Class D and the overseer(s), the testing shall be concluded and the Class-D is to be taken back to their cell, after an optional interview that can be called by the overseer(s).

Note: SCP-5127 will not affect anyone in photographic or video form, nor in artistic depictions.


Interview: 

+Open

-Close


D-Class personnel:  Holy shit, man, what the hell happened? I feel all woozy and shit!

Dr. Kyesha:  Relax. You’re here for a checkup.

D-Class personnel:  A checkup? You mean, like, at a doctor?

Dr. Kyesha:  Sure. So getting into this, what particular emotions are you feeling currently?

D-Class personnel:  Uh, I feel pretty tired. And like I’m gonna throw up.

[Dr. Kyesha takes notes on his clipboard]

Dr. Kyesha:  I see. Anything else? We have bags if you’d like.

D-Class personnel:  Thanks doc, I think I’m okay though. Um, well I did have a headache when I woke up on that sofa. By the way, why was I asleep?

Dr. Kyesha:  From what we understand, you weren’t asleep.

D-Class personnel:  This is so trippy, man. I just wanna know what’s going on.

Dr. Kyesha:  So do we. Remember, we’re trying to find out what’s going on. Focus your brain. What do you remember?

[D-Class sighs]

D-Class personnel:  Well, um, I remember this guy escorting me inside this small room. As soon as I entered, I woke up here on this sofa.

Dr. Kyesha:  Interesting.

[Dr. Kyesha takes more notes]

D-Class personnel:  So, uh, I don’t know if I can ask you this, but when can I go back home?

[Dr. Kyesha smiles]

Dr. Kyesha:  Got a homesick one, have we? Listen buddy, if you do what we tell you to, we might even let you go back early. Now, is this it? Is there anything else?

D-Class personnel:  No man. I told you everything I know.

[Dr. Kyesha signals the security camera]

Dr. Kyesha:  Well then, that concludes our interview. Please fill out these papers, I’ll come back in fifteen minutes to collect them. Should you have any questions, please keep them until I come back. Good day.

[Dr. Kyesha leaves the room and closes the door behind himself]

[After the interview]

[Dr. Kyesha is approached by Dr. ██████ ]

Dr. Kyesha:  Well, from what I understand, this flower affects memory.]

Dr. █████ :  Can you be more specific?

**Dr. Kyesha: Of course. I’m just getting into it. Let’s go to my office.

Dr. █████ :  What about the Class D? Is he cooperating?

**Dr. Kyesha: Gah, it’s like talking to an infant. A stoner, most likely, in his past life. He’s giving us all he can, but due to the nature of this subject, he can’t recollect much.

Dr. █████ :  Good to know. Let’s continue in the office.

[Interview end, time 12:39 a.m.]


